;; expect: main.apart refused pattern_type
;; §8.4 slice 3.18 rule 1: a row's representation is not an E-first body's to read. A ByteArray
;; runs as Init's List cells, and this body — E-first: it quotes a symbol — would take it apart
;; with List's constructors; the classifier's pass refuses every constructor pattern on a row's
;; type, as the elaborator does on the typed route (pattern_constructor), so the lowering may
;; give the type another layout behind the same signatures. An `if` on one is if_type
(import Init String.toByteArray)
(fn apart ((b ByteArray)) Nat (match (quote k) (_ (match b (List.nil 0) ((List.cons h t) h)))))
